; Independent review of both reciprocal-choice observations and their linked
; interpretation. The shared review flow persists each answer before collection.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "docs/coherence-substrate/reciprocal-choice-microkernel-two-observations-review.md"
  "Review this executable two-observation candidate adversarially and independently; do not edit any file. Separate mechanical trace evidence from semantic interpretation. For OBSERVATION 1, assess whether do and step budget 3 were selected by the declared transparent charge policy and whether the fragment/interrupt claims follow. For OBSERVATION 2, assess whether see and step budget 5 were selected by that policy, whether mutually bounded channel budget 4 follows, and whether the carried human choice preserves rather than fabricates sovereignty. Then assess the LINK: does the trace establish a do-to-see mode switch and receiver/channel budget changes, while honestly stopping short of biological intuition, independent measurement, or real model-logit interception? Assess whether form-neutral state ID 1 with the audible NL surface humm is represented as a state rather than a fourth mode. Examine whether the remaining intuition source label is too strong, whether declared-charge-policy-selected and fixture-calibration-met avoid circular overclaim, whether any step budget is still mislabeled as wall-clock timeout, and whether the two-turn protocol actually leaves a fresh choice point. Return: OVERALL VERDICT (PASS, REVISE, or BLOCK); separate verdicts for observation 1, observation 2, and the linked inference; claims permitted verbatim; claims that must be rejected or renamed; the three most important located objections; and the smallest executable repair required before calling this healthy.")
